---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---
<SiteLayout title="About — Simon Gelbart" current="about">
  <section class="page-heading narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1>A simple map of the work.</h1>
    <p class="lede">I’m Simon Gelbart, a senior backend developer in France. I work mostly with .NET and C#, with a focus on systems that are understandable, testable, and able to evolve.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">What you’ll find here</p>
      <h2>Projects in different stages.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="about-copy">
      <p>Some repositories are libraries or tools. Others are experiments, learning material, or practical work around backend development.</p>
      <p>I’m not presenting them as finished products. The useful part is the trail: the code, the tests, the decisions, and the things I learn while making them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split section-rule">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Main interests</p>
      <h2>Where I tend to spend time.</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="interest-list">
      <li>Backend architecture and domain modeling</li>
      <li>.NET and C# API design</li>
      <li>Testing, integration environments, and reliability</li>
      <li>Developer tools and AI-assisted workflows</li>
      <li>Teaching through examples and small decisions</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="follow-card">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Keep exploring</p>
      <h2>See the source, not just the summary.</h2>
    </div>
    <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/SimonGelbart" rel="noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
